adata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-2k","agent_clan_generation":"20260929134516","approve":true,"bead_id":"bob-cli-2k.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-2k[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Choose each Task Link's outcome while closing a Pomodoro with [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]=x<N>!<M>[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]`=x<N>`, `=x!<M>`, and `=x<N>!<M>` close the running Pomodoro and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]decide, by number, which of its Task Links stay in progress, which [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]are deferred, and which are completed and struck. This does in one [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]capture what the user does by hand before Ctrl+Enter: append `#` to[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]links that should not start, and transclude links whose tasks are [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]finished. Every close stays atomic. A mistyped list gets a precise [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]diagnostic. Plain `=x` keeps working byte for byte as it does [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]today. `bob capture` output and the Bob Mac Capture close card show[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]a number badge on every Task Link and the outcome each one will [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]get, so choosing the numbers is easy.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]close_task_selection.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/close_task_selection.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-2k[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-2k/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Numbered Task Links and outcome selection in the pure close [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]planner[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]selection-planner[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selection-planner: in `src/native/capture_pomodoro_close/`, number the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]running[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]session's Task Links. Apply a `CloseSelection` by rewriting only the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`#`/`![[…]]`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]markers of the numbered lines, then run the unchanged close. Validate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]numbers[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against the lineup, warn when a listed task cannot change status, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expose the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]numbered lineup plus a per-row `index`. Every caller passes `None` for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]now. Pinned[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]by unit tests on the worked example.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]=x<N>!<M> grammar, capture-parse contract, and editor states[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]selection-grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selection-grammar: lex `=x[<N>][!<M>]` once and share the lexer between [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whole-item close and the `@`/`^`/body-bearing `=x` suffix, in both the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]execution[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and editor parsers. Report the additive `in_progress`/`complete` spec, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new span[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kinds, precise `invalid_pomodoro_close` diagnostics, and an incomplete[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`pomodoro_close_task` need for a dangling `,`/`!`. Update [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-complete,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-rewrite, and capture-parse help. The executor refuses a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]selection-bearing[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]close until selection-capture wires it in.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wire the selection into all close forms, JSON, and human [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]output[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]selection-capture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after selection-planner, selection-grammar[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selection-capture: pass the parsed selection into the planner for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whole-item,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]link, and new-task closes, and remove the temporary refusal. Emit[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`in_progress`, `complete`, `task_links`, and `tasks[].index` in the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`pomodoro_close` JSON. Print a numbered index column in human output, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and fix the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`carries 1 links` plural. Pin all of it with CLI integration tests on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the worked[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]example, including batches, link forms, dry-run parity, and every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostic.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Help and docs for =x<N>!<M>[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]selection-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after selection-capture[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selection-docs: document the selection grammar, numbering, outcomes,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics, and the JSON and human output. Update `bob capture --help`,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`docs/capture.md` (grammar tables, the close section with worked [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]examples, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the capture-parse, capture, and capture-complete contracts), and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`README.md`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture numbered close card, span colors, and pending [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]list state[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-selection-preview[dim] · [dim][/dim]after selection-capture[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-selection-preview: in the bob-mac-capture linked repo, decode the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new close[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fields. Render SF Symbol number badges tinted by outcome on the close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]card, with[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a teaching hint before a selection is typed and an outcome summary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]after. Color[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the in-progress and complete list spans in the editor. Keep a live, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dimmed card[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with Close disabled while a list ends in `,` or `!`. Update status and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notifications, regenerate real-bob fixtures, add tests and README notes,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and get[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]macOS CI green.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-2k","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-2k.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-738dedbdd4b7cb893c4854262babfab0","started_at":"2026-09-29T13:45:25.313022","state":"dismissed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1790705759,"sha":"1838779284b63937735b988a4f09e57d7ae50325","subject":"feat(capture): add pomodoro close selection grammar"}],"dismissed_at":"2026-09-29T14:16:44.194382","files":{"chat":{"digest":"abb70242a60762ba040e22bdec597dbfd760e1ffd8b3abefd61759d9f3e7ca51","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-2k.2/chat.md","size_bytes":3715},"commits":{"digest":"0a3abb531182c84bcccd6f30ee872423b3b06c0325af50bd68485050925647de","path":"agents/b